[{"id":1,"domain":"repo_health","question":"A friend asks whether they should contribute to weatherly. What do you tell them?","type":"single","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Yes, the open PRs show people are engaged here.","correct":false,"explanation":"The contributors are engaged, but the maintainer isn't. Open PRs only mean people tried — they say nothing about whether anyone is reviewing."},{"id":"b","text":"No, nobody seems to be reviewing PRs here.","correct":true,"explanation":"The most recent merged PR is over a year old, four PRs are sitting open with no response, and the maintainer hasn't replied anywhere in almost a year. That's the clearest signal you can get."},{"id":"c","text":"Not sure — wait and see if #22 gets answered.","correct":false,"explanation":"Issue #22 has been open for weeks with no reply. The silence is already your answer."},{"id":"d","text":"Yes, #5 is labelled good first issue.","correct":false,"explanation":"Labels are set by maintainers and can be years old. This one was set about 16 months ago when the project was still active."}]},{"id":2,"domain":"repo_health","question":"Which two signals are the strongest evidence that nobody will review your PR? (Select two)","type":"multi","options":[{"id":"a","text":"There is no CONTRIBUTING.md.","correct":false,"explanation":"Many small, healthy repos have no CONTRIBUTING.md. Absence of it alone doesn't signal abandonment."},{"id":"b","text":"The most recent merged PR is over a year old.","correct":true,"explanation":"If nothing has been merged in over a year, there is no evidence the maintainer is still reviewing anything."},{"id":"c","text":"There are open PRs.","correct":false,"explanation":"Busy, healthy repos have plenty of open PRs. Open PRs alone mean nothing — you need to look at whether they get responses."},{"id":"d","text":"The maintainer's last reply anywhere is almost a year old.","correct":true,"explanation":"If the maintainer hasn't replied to any issue or PR in almost a year, there is no reason to expect they will reply to yours."},{"id":"e","text":"#5 has a good first issue label.","correct":false,"explanation":"A label says nothing about whether anyone is reviewing. Labels are set once and rarely updated."}]},{"id":3,"domain":"issue_judgment","question":"You've decided to contribute to weatherly. Which issue would you take?","type":"single","options":[{"id":"a","text":"#2 — Crash when the city isn't found.","correct":false,"explanation":"This is a real, reproducible bug. But check the open PRs first — a fix has been sitting in PR #19 for 9 months with no response from the maintainer."},{"id":"b","text":"#5 — Add Fahrenheit option.","correct":false,"explanation":"The label is about 16 months old and nobody is reviewing PRs. The change being small doesn't help if there's nobody to merge it."},{"id":"c","text":"#7 — IndexError when the weather list is empty.","correct":false,"explanation":"A real bug, but someone claimed it in November and opened no PR since. Always ask before starting on a claimed issue."},{"id":"d","text":"#20 — API key invalid?","correct":false,"explanation":"No steps, no version, no traceback. There is not enough information to reproduce this, let alone fix it."},{"id":"e","text":"None of these — I'd look for a different repo.","correct":true,"explanation":"Every issue here has a problem: the repo is abandoned, fixes go unmerged, issues are claimed without follow-up, or reports lack enough information. The right call is to walk away."}]},{"id":4,"domain":"issue_judgment","question":"You've reproduced issue #2 and want to fix it. What do you check first?","type":"single","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Whether a fix already exists somewhere in the repo.","correct":true,"explanation":"PR #19 has had a correct fix sitting open for 9 months. Writing the same fix again would duplicate work that is already being ignored."},{"id":"b","text":"Whether your Python version matches the maintainer's.","correct":false,"explanation":"Python version matters for compatibility, but it has no bearing on whether a fix already exists."},{"id":"c","text":"Whether the original reporter has contributed elsewhere.","correct":false,"explanation":"The reporter's contribution history is irrelevant to whether you should open a duplicate fix."},{"id":"d","text":"How many reactions the issue has.","correct":false,"explanation":"Reaction counts tell you how many people want a fix, not whether one already exists or whether anyone will review yours."}]},{"id":5,"domain":"issue_judgment","question":"Issue #5 is labelled good first issue and the change is small. What is the real problem with taking it?","type":"single","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Small changes need a test first.","correct":false,"explanation":"Tests are good practice, but they aren't the reason this issue is a bad pick."},{"id":"b","text":"Fahrenheit conversion is too hard for beginners.","correct":false,"explanation":"The conversion itself is straightforward. Difficulty isn't the issue here."},{"id":"c","text":"Nobody is around to review it.","correct":true,"explanation":"The maintainer wrote this label about 16 months ago when the project was active. A good first issue label only helps if someone is there to review the PR. There isn't."},{"id":"d","text":"The label only applies to documentation issues.","correct":false,"explanation":"Good first issue applies to any kind of contribution. The label itself isn't the problem."}]},{"id":6,"domain":"repo_health","question":"Issue #2 says parse_weather crashes when the city isn't found. You call it with a normal weather response and it works fine. What do you do next?","type":"single","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Mark it \"Can't reproduce\" — it works on my machine.","correct":false,"explanation":"You didn't use the input described in the report. A normal response isn't the failing case."},{"id":"b","text":"Re-run it with the not-found response the report describes.","correct":true,"explanation":"\"Can't reproduce\" only counts after you follow the reporter's exact steps. The crash happens with a not-found response, not a valid one."},{"id":"c","text":"Mark it \"Reproduced\" — the report is detailed enough to trust.","correct":false,"explanation":"Trusting the report without running the steps isn't reproducing. You need to confirm it yourself."},{"id":"d","text":"Comment \"works for me\" and move on.","correct":false,"explanation":"You tested the wrong input. This comment would be wrong and unhelpful."}]},{"id":7,"domain":"contributing","question":"You've decided weatherly isn't worth your time. What's the best next move?","type":"single","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Open a PR anyway to show interest.","correct":false,"explanation":"A PR on an abandoned repo wastes your time and adds noise. It won't get reviewed."},{"id":"b","text":"Comment on #22 and wait for an answer.","correct":false,"explanation":"Issue #22 has already been open for weeks with no reply. Waiting costs you weeks more on a project that's shown no signs of life."},{"id":"c","text":"Fork it and maintain it yourself.","correct":false,"explanation":"Maintaining a fork is a months-long commitment. It's a valid path eventually, but not a first-contribution move."},{"id":"d","text":"Apply the same checks to a different project.","correct":true,"explanation":"Moving on isn't failing — it's the skill this repo is here to teach. You just saved yourself weeks of work on a dead end."}]},{"id":8,"domain":"review","question":"Look at PR #16. Who is the conversation waiting on?","type":"single","options":[{"id":"a","text":"The maintainer.","correct":true,"explanation":"The maintainer asked for a test. The author added it the same day and said so. Everything the author was asked to do is done — the ball is entirely in the maintainer's court."},{"id":"b","text":"The author, who still has changes to make.","correct":false,"explanation":"The author replied the same day the changes were requested and confirmed the test was added. There is nothing left for them to do."},{"id":"c","text":"A second reviewer.","correct":false,"explanation":"There is no mention of a second reviewer being required. The thread only involves the maintainer and the author."},{"id":"d","text":"Nobody — it's approved and ready to merge.","correct":false,"explanation":"The maintainer never replied after the author added the test. It has not been approved."}]}]