[{"id":1,"domain":"repo_health","question":"Which two signals best suggest a PR here would actually get reviewed?","type":"multi","options":[{"id":"a","text":"The repo has plenty of stars.","correct":false,"explanation":"Stars show popularity, not review speed. A repo can have thousands of stars and an inactive maintainer."},{"id":"b","text":"PRs get merged within days.","correct":true,"explanation":"PR #5 merged in 3 days, #7 in 2, #8 in 4. That pattern tells you the maintainer is actively reviewing."},{"id":"c","text":"The README is short.","correct":false,"explanation":"README length says nothing about how quickly PRs get reviewed."},{"id":"d","text":"Issues get replies within a day or two.","correct":true,"explanation":"The maintainer replied to issue #6 the next day and to #9 the day after it was opened. That response time carries over to PRs."},{"id":"e","text":"A LICENSE file exists.","correct":false,"explanation":"A license sets reuse rights, not response times."}]},{"id":2,"domain":"repo_health","question":"What do the review comments on this repo's merged PRs suggest your PR should include?","type":"single","options":[{"id":"a","text":"A screenshot of the output.","correct":false,"explanation":"This is a calculation library — there's nothing visual to screenshot."},{"id":"b","text":"A changelog entry.","correct":false,"explanation":"There's no changelog file in the repo."},{"id":"c","text":"Tests covering your change.","correct":true,"explanation":"The maintainer asked for tests in PR #8 before merging. That's the clearest signal of what they expect."},{"id":"d","text":"A link to an issue in the PR title.","correct":false,"explanation":"PR #5 fixed issue #3 and was merged without ever mentioning the issue number in the title. The maintainer didn't flag it."}]},{"id":3,"domain":"issue_judgment","question":"Which issue would you take?","type":"single","options":[{"id":"a","text":"#2 — Support 4.0 GPA scale.","correct":false,"explanation":"Labelled easy, but the thread lists three different 4.0 mappings and nobody has chosen one. You can't write the code until that decision is made."},{"id":"b","text":"#3 — KeyError when using grade 'A+'.","correct":false,"explanation":"This was fixed by PR #5 in June. The issue tracker was never updated because the PR didn't link it. Try the code before you start."},{"id":"c","text":"#6 — cgpa() ignores credit weights.","correct":false,"explanation":"The bug is confirmed and real, but it was assigned to another contributor on 2026-09-07. Check before stepping in."},{"id":"d","text":"#9 — CGPA looks wrong sometimes.","correct":false,"explanation":"No inputs, no expected vs actual values. The maintainer asked for more details and got no follow-up. You can't reproduce it."},{"id":"e","text":"#10 — semester_gpa([]) raises ZeroDivisionError.","correct":true,"explanation":"Confirmed by the maintainer, the fix is spelled out in the thread, unclaimed, and a test is explicitly requested. Everything you need is there."}]},{"id":4,"domain":"issue_judgment","question":"How much weight should the 'good first issue' label carry when you choose?","type":"single","options":[{"id":"a","text":"A lot — maintainers only add it to genuinely easy issues.","correct":false,"explanation":"Labels reflect someone's opinion at the time they were added. Issue #2 has that label and hides an unresolved design question."},{"id":"b","text":"Some — use it as a first filter, but read the thread to confirm.","correct":true,"explanation":"The label is a useful starting point, not a guarantee. The thread is where you find out if the label still holds."},{"id":"c","text":"None — labels are only guesses.","correct":false,"explanation":"Labels are still a useful first filter. Ignoring them entirely slows you down."},{"id":"d","text":"Only if the issue also has the bug label.","correct":false,"explanation":"The bug label says what kind of issue it is. It says nothing about how hard it is to fix."}]},{"id":5,"domain":"issue_judgment","question":"Issue #9 says the CGPA \"sometimes\" differs from the college portal. What do you need before you could even try to reproduce it?","type":"single","options":[{"id":"a","text":"The reporter's operating system.","correct":false,"explanation":"This is plain Python arithmetic. The OS rarely affects the result."},{"id":"b","text":"Which college they attend.","correct":false,"explanation":"Knowing the college might help you guess the grading scale, but you still can't run anything without the actual inputs."},{"id":"c","text":"A screenshot of the portal page.","correct":false,"explanation":"That shows the number they expected, not what inputs produced the wrong one."},{"id":"d","text":"The exact grades and credits they entered.","correct":true,"explanation":"Without the inputs you can't call the function, and without calling the function you can't compare outputs. That's the minimum needed — and it might also reveal whether this is just the weighting bug from #6."}]},{"id":6,"domain":"issue_judgment","question":"You follow an old bug report's steps on the current code and nothing goes wrong. What do you do?","type":"single","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Mark \"Can't reproduce\", then look for a related fix in the PR history.","correct":true,"explanation":"That's the right call. Issue #3 was confirmed in May on the old code, then fixed by PR #5 on June 2. Running the steps today gives you 9.0 with no error."},{"id":"b","text":"Mark \"Reproduced\" — others confirmed it earlier.","correct":false,"explanation":"Those confirmations described the code at the time. You need to reproduce it on the current code."},{"id":"c","text":"Reinstall everything, assuming your setup is broken.","correct":false,"explanation":"The steps were clear and ran without error. Your setup is probably fine — the bug is gone."},{"id":"d","text":"Mark \"Not enough info\" — the report is too old to trust.","correct":false,"explanation":"An old report can still have complete steps. Age doesn't make it incomplete."}]},{"id":7,"domain":"contributing","question":"Issue #6 was assigned to another contributor a week ago and has no PR yet. You'd still like to work on it. What's the best move?","type":"single","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Start now and open your PR first.","correct":false,"explanation":"That duplicates someone else's work and creates an awkward situation for the maintainer."},{"id":"b","text":"Ask the maintainer to reassign it to you.","correct":false,"explanation":"The maintainer assigned it on purpose. A week is too soon to ask for it back."},{"id":"c","text":"Leave it to them and choose another issue.","correct":true,"explanation":"A week is not long enough to assume someone has dropped it. Issue #10 is unclaimed and confirmed — start there."},{"id":"d","text":"Comment asking if they've given up.","correct":false,"explanation":"That reads as impatient after just one week. If the assignee had been silent for months, a polite check-in would be reasonable."}]},{"id":8,"domain":"review","question":"The maintainer asks you to make an empty semester return 0.0, but you think raising an error is cleaner. What do you do?","type":"single","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Push your version and explain it's cleaner.","correct":false,"explanation":"That ignores a direct request from the person who owns the project."},{"id":"b","text":"Close the PR and open another with your version.","correct":false,"explanation":"That throws away the review thread and starts the cycle over."},{"id":"c","text":"Keep arguing in the thread until they agree.","correct":false,"explanation":"Repeated arguments cost goodwill and delay the merge. Make your case once."},{"id":"d","text":"Share your reasoning once, then follow their call.","correct":true,"explanation":"The maintainer owns the project's behaviour contract. They've already said what they want in the issue thread. You can note your view — once — but the decision is theirs."}]}]